[
  {"comment": "Infinite Canvas is part of the Page Edges icon, so the Page Edges element is switched on on the Elements page, a fresh bar hiding it, and a press on the middle steps Fixed, Grows, Wraps Sides and Wraps All Edges. A press on the left column takes the wrap from off to Sides Only, and one on the top row from there to All Edges. The bar then shows one icon, the grid of nine, with no arrow beside it. From each of the three wraps, off, Sides Only and All Edges, the icon is shot with the pointer away, and then with the pointer over the left column, the top row, the top left corner, the right column, the bottom row and the middle, each hover drawing in a fainter tone the cells the press there would leave, or none where the press turns the wrap off. The state dump after each press reads the wrap. The dockers are parked first, so no click lands on one."},
  {"docker": "park"},
  {"wait": 45},
